message: "If you use this framework or case study evidence, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Ad Quality Evaluation Framework: A Rubric-Based Methodology for Search Advertising Quality Assessment"
authors:
  - family-names: "Palencia Robles"
    given-names: "Diego"
    affiliation: "Universidad Galileo"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
repository-code: "https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/ad-quality-evaluation-framework"
abstract: >
  A rubric-based framework for evaluating the relevance and quality of search
  advertisements, grounded in search intent theory, Google's Quality Score
  methodology, and applied Decision Intelligence. Contains three empirical case
  studies: live ad quality evaluation, search campaign blueprint, and keyword
  intent mapping.
keywords:
  - ad quality evaluation
  - search intent
  - Quality Score
  - decision intelligence
  - Google Ads
  - keyword match types
  - inter-rater reliability
